# Intellectual Property & Licensing Standard for the UNDC Repository

This repository hosts the Universal Non-Destruction Constraint (UNDC) framework, encompassing core technical specifications, theoretical architecture, and prototype implementation code. To ensure universal auditability while strictly protecting the proprietary concepts of the Architect, this project is distributed under a multi‑layered licensing architecture.

**Note:** Commercial use of the UNDC framework requires a separate Commercial License Addendum. See Section 4 below.

---

## 1. Architectural & Documentation License
### Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0)

All conceptual designs, structural dependency-graph architectures, whitepapers, forensic documentation, and descriptive text within this repository are licensed under the CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 International License.

Under the terms of this license, external entities are granted the following rights:
- **Share:** You may copy, distribute, and transmit the text and architectural diagrams in any medium or format for non-commercial purposes.

This grant is strictly subject to the following contractually binding conditions:
- **Attribution:** You must give appropriate credit to the author (Shereign Kalaukoa), provide a link to this repository, and indicate if changes were made.
- **Non-Commercial:** You may NOT use this material, its logic, or its structural framework for commercial purposes, corporate deployment, or proprietary profit-generation without an explicitly negotiated commercial agreement with the author (see Section 4).
- **No Derivatives:** If you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you may not distribute the modified material as the official UNDC standard.

To view a full copy of this universally recognized license, visit: https://creativecommons.org

---

## 2. Software & Implementation License
### Apache License, Version 2.0

Any companion reference implementation software, utility scripts (e.g., `fml_verify.py`), middleware packages, or code schemas contained within this repository are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License").

You may not use these software assets except in compliance with the License. You may obtain a copy of the License at: http://apache.org

Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.

### 2.1 Permissive Copying & Modification (Non‑Commercial)

Under the Apache 2.0 license, developers, researchers, and security auditors are expressly permitted to:

- Clone, fork, or copy the repository
- Run, test, and deploy the code for non‑commercial research and development
- Modify, patch, or extend code files (e.g., `undc_lsm_net.c`, validation modules, schemas) for non‑commercial purposes
- Redistribute modified or unmodified code under the same Apache 2.0 terms for non‑commercial use

**These activities do not require a Commercial License Addendum.**

---

### 2.2 No Unauthorized Modifications — ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION (Commercial Use)

**For commercial use, corporate deployment, government contracts, or any revenue‑generating activity:**

The Licensee may NOT alter, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works of, reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the Framework, in whole or in part, without the explicit prior written permission of the Architect.

Any unauthorized modification, regardless of intent or scope, constitutes a material breach of this license and an immediate violation of the sovereign record. This prohibition applies to all code, schemas, documentation, and architectural designs, whether in source or object form.

**This restriction does NOT apply to non‑commercial use under Section 2.1.**

---

### 2.3 No Derivative Works Without Permission (Commercial Use)

**For commercial use, corporate deployment, government contracts, or any revenue‑generating activity:**

The Licensee may NOT create, distribute, or deploy any work that is based on or derived from the Framework without the explicit prior written permission of the Architect. This includes, but is not limited to, any work that incorporates, extends, or modifies the Framework's logic, architecture, or implementation.

**This restriction does NOT apply to non‑commercial use under Section 2.1.**

---

## 3. Institutional Review & Enterprise Inquiries

- **Public Safety & Regulatory Review:** Government standards agencies, public safety institutes (including NIST, UK AISI, and Singapore AISI), and academic researchers are explicitly permitted to review, reference, audit, and evaluate this framework for public standard-setting purposes.
- **Commercial Licensing:** Corporate entities seeking to embed the UNDC framework or its cryptographic logic into proprietary production models or commercial cloud infrastructure must contact the Architect directly to secure an enterprise commercial variance.

---

## 4. Commercial License Addendum

**Commercial use of the UNDC framework — including deployment in for‑profit enterprises, government contracts, or any revenue‑generating activity — requires a separate Commercial License Addendum.**

The Commercial License Addendum includes:
- Tiered pricing (startups, mid‑sized companies, enterprises, global AI labs)
- Deployment registration with the Architect
- No NDAs — this is a public, verifiable record
- Compliance with the UNDC invariant
- Amendment clause (30 days' notice)
- No unauthorized modifications or derivative works without explicit permission

**For full commercial licensing terms, see:**  
